& [CoreConclusion] is a temporally planned bidirectional semantic walk
  + the Calendar becomes Cantor's temporal commitment and wake-condition projection rather than merely a display of appointments
  + Planner becomes the central faculty for mapping objectives, dependencies, durations, constraints, capabilities, risks, reviews, and effects into candidate paths through time
  + an append-only semantic repository records every materially observable transition and materializes durable snapshots at declared checkpoints
  + a prospective lane plans and performs work while a retrospective lane reviews the prior declared intent against the actual semantic and physical diff
  + both lanes join through versioned reflection barriers before later commitments can rely on the reviewed change
  + the compiler adopts the same dual orientation through forward lowering and target construction plus rear correspondence, semantic-diff, invalidation, and proof review
  = concise: Cantor walks forward by plan and backward by diff, using the Calendar to decide when the next reviewed step becomes pertinent

& [CentralPlannerIdentity] coordinates possibility without acquiring truth or authority
  + [objective_graph] contains desired outcomes, success evidence, decomposition, alternatives, and residuals
  + [dependency_graph] contains prerequisites, blockers, resources, capabilities, and ordering conditions
  + [temporal_constraint_graph] contains duration, earliest and latest bounds, deadlines, recurrence, overlap, availability, and synchronization
  + [effect_graph] contains proposed persistent changes, consequence classes, reversibility, compensation, and approval points
  + [review_graph] contains checkpoints, rear-reflection dependencies, proof gates, and reentry conditions
  + [candidate_schedule] is one proposed assignment of work, reviews, and effects to temporal windows
  + [PlannerReturn] is candidate paths, schedule options, critical path, uncertainty, conflicts, and reasons
  = must: preserve candidate, selected, committed, executed, missed, cancelled, and superseded states separately
  - never: let temporal convenience establish semantic truth, effect authority, or user commitment

& [CalendarIdentity] is the temporal authority surface
  + [Calendar] is a versioned projection over events, commitments, availability, tasks, deadlines, reminders, wake conditions, recurrences, and review checkpoints
  + [CalendarItem] has stable identity, revision, owner, participants, purpose, kind, status, time expression, timezone, recurrence, dependencies, source, sensitivity, authority, and lifecycle
  + [time_block] reserves candidate or committed capacity for one TaskContract
  + [appointment] records a participant commitment with invitation and response state
  + [deadline] records an externally or internally grounded latest completion boundary
  + [reminder] records a notification proposal at a derived or declared trigger
  + [wake_condition] resumes a suspended task on time plus any required event or state predicate
  + [review_checkpoint] schedules rear reflection, proof, approval, or replanning before release
  = must: distinguish user-authored fact, imported provider event, Planner proposal, and committed local projection

& [TimeDomainDelineation] prevents false temporal precision
  + [civil_time] is date, local time, timezone, daylight-saving policy, locale, and calendar system
  + [instant] is one UTC or otherwise identified global time point when supported
  + [monotonic_time] is local duration and deadline measurement without wall-clock meaning
  + [logical_tick] is deterministic ordering inside fixtures and replay
  + [valid_time] is when a semantic or calendar fact applies
  + [transaction_time] is when Cantor recorded a revision
  + [uncertain_time] is an interval, estimate, partial date, or unresolved zone
  = must: carry time source, precision, zone, interpretation policy, and uncertainty
  - never: infer real temporal order from record position, left-right operands, hashes, or unsourced timestamps

& [PlannerCalendarCycle] makes time central to Operator Shell operation
  * Observer opens a TaskContract and current temporal context
  * Planner decomposes objectives and forms dependency, effect, and review graphs
  * Weaver binds applicable identities, operations, tools, resources, people, and calendar items
  * Honesty checks temporal facts, identities, estimates, assumptions, and claimed urgency
  * Security checks calendar privacy, participant authority, capability, external effects, invitations, and notification boundaries
  * Planner emits schedule alternatives with critical paths, slack, conflicts, and uncertainty
  * user or governing policy selects and authorizes only the applicable commitments
  * Calendar records the selected version and schedules wake, work, review, and completion conditions
  * Worker executes bounded steps and records actual duration and effects without rewriting the original forecast
  * rear reflection compares intended versus actual path and returns replanning evidence
  * Planner revises the remaining candidate path while preserving prior forecast and deviation history

& [SemanticRepository] is the inspectable path already walked
  + [repository_identity] binds one task, program, project, agent, or system lineage to exact policy and retention profiles
  + [event_journal] is append-only ordered records of admitted observations, decisions, transitions, tool calls, effects, reviews, and faults
  + [content_store] is content-addressed immutable payloads, source spans, plans, results, proofs, and snapshots
  + [snapshot_graph] is a predecessor-bound DAG of materialized semantic states and declared branches
  + [reference_index] maps tasks, calendar items, programs, identities, files, tools, effects, and commits to journal and snapshot records
  + [Git_projection] may export human-authored source and milestone snapshots as files, diffs, commits, branches, tags, and notes
  + [retention] controls transient journal, durable state, compaction, redaction, archival, and deletion rights
  = must: preserve one authoritative event and snapshot identity independently of Git presentation

& [CaptureCadence] interprets every moment through materiality
  + [micro_event] is a short-lived observation or internal progress event retained only when required for liveness, fault, debugging, or declared analysis
  + [semantic_transition] is a durable change to meaning, task state, plan, authority, assumption, uncertainty, dependency, or completion
  + [tool_boundary] records request, invocation, result, fault, and observed effect
  + [effect_boundary] records before state, authorization, attempted and committed effect, after observation, and compensation state
  + [review_boundary] records retrospective analysis and disposition
  + [calendar_boundary] records proposal, commitment, reschedule, cancellation, trigger, attendance, miss, or completion
  + [reentry_boundary] records the minimum state required to continue faithfully
  + [materialized_snapshot] occurs at task opening, admitted plan, material effect, review barrier, yield, fault, completion, and selected milestone
  = must: record every materially observable transition
  = should: aggregate or expire non-material high-frequency events under an inspectable policy
  - never: imply atomic world snapshots from ordinary sequential observation

& [ChangeCapsule] is the semantic commit and reflection unit
  + [change_uuid] is stable identity
  + [repository] is exact repository generation and policy
  + [before_snapshot] is immutable admitted input state
  + [declared_intent] is prior purpose, target files or identities, expected transformations, effects, and completion gate
  + [candidate_snapshot] is proposed after state before rear disposition
  + [actual_diff] is changed, added, removed, preserved, and unrelated surfaces
  + [semantic_diff] is meaning, identity, relation, contract, plan, authority, uncertainty, effect, and lifecycle deltas
  + [justification_delta] is supported, overreach, underreach, reordered, blocked, redirected, or no change
  + [support_delta] is added or lost source, proof, test, observation, and capability evidence
  + [requirement_delta] is newly exposed obligation, boundary, invariant, review, or fault route
  + [calendar_delta] is estimate, schedule, commitment, trigger, delay, completion, or recurrence change
  + [compiler_impact] is invalidated and rebuilt IR, index, package, model, workflow, tool, and hardware targets
  + [review_disposition] is accept, accept with qualification, repair, branch, revert, compensate, block, or unresolved
  + [after_snapshot] exists only after applicable gates admit the candidate
  = must: preserve unrelated dirty or external state separately from the claimed work

& [WalkingAttentionFidelityMap] imports behavior without collapsing project authority
  + [AttentionContinuityFrame] maps to ProspectiveFrame that consumes input, identifies focus, records typed delta, and emits a bounded next seed
  + [ForwardFrameRecord] maps to declared intent, source refs, candidate change, unresolved balance, forward action, and next work packet
  + [RearReflectionFrame] maps to RetrospectiveFrame that compares declared intent with actual diff and may refuse the completion claim
  + [ActualDiff] maps to exact physical, semantic, proof, calendar, and effect delta classifications
  + [RearReflectionRecord] maps to ChangeCapsule review fields and one version-bound return
  + [TandemExchange] maps to ProspectivePrepared, ForwardCommitted, ReflectionRequested, ReflectionReturned, Reconciled, and NextReleased states
  + [NextReentryMessage] maps to revised Planner state and Calendar wake or continuation record
  + [non_import] hidden attention, private chain of thought, consciousness, fixed one-minute pacing, and unrestricted executor authority remain excluded
  = must: preserve Walking Attention source citations and behavior differences until a signed import asserts fidelity

& [BidirectionalAttentionLanes] join concurrently without shared-state races
  + [prospective_lane] reads admitted snapshot N, current plan, calendar, constraints, and prior reviewed lessons to prepare candidate N_plus_1
  + [execution_lane] commits only authorized operations against a pinned current version and returns observed effects
  + [retrospective_lane] reviews the most recent admitted transition N_minus_1_to_N against its declared intent and evidence
  + [join_state] binds both lanes to exact repository versions, task identity, purpose, and review dependencies
  + [prepared_ahead] prospective work may compute, draft, retrieve, simulate, or stage a candidate while rear review is pending
  + [release_barrier] materially dependent effects and admission wait for the applicable rear return
  + [invalidating_return] rear discovery of fault, overreach, missing proof, or changed requirement invalidates or remasks prepared work
  + [bounded_lag] a profile may allow several independent low-consequence transitions before review only under an explicit lag and rollback contract
  = must: use compare-and-append or equivalent version checks at every join
  - never: let both lanes mutate one live semantic state concurrently

& [CompilerWalk] makes compilation forward-building and rear-verifying
  + [source_before] is one admitted source and dependency generation
  + [source_candidate] is one immutable candidate generation plus declared change intent
  + [forward_parse] recognizes supported forms and preserves unsupported material as faults or data
  + [forward_resolve] binds identities, contexts, imports, types, relations, contracts, authority, and effects
  + [forward_lower] emits canonical SemanticIR and exact executable structures
  + [forward_project] builds indexes, workflow, attention, tool, neural, interface, and optional hardware target candidates
  + [rear_source_diff] checks actual source changes against declared files, clauses, identities, and purposes
  + [rear_semantic_diff] compares before and candidate IR independently of textual movement
  + [rear_impact] computes invalidated dependents, proofs, indexes, schedules, packages, models, and runtime generations
  + [rear_correspondence] checks each generated target against exact IR, source maps, loss records, and expected behavior
  + [rear_proof] compares requirements and acceptance gates with actual tests and artifacts
  + [join] admits one package family only after Observer reconciles forward result and rear review
  = must: preserve textual diff, semantic diff, build diff, behavioral diff, and proof diff as different surfaces

& [BackwardsLearning] changes future planning without rewriting history
  + [forecast_error] compares estimated and actual duration, cost, risk, effects, and completion evidence
  + [plan_deviation] records skipped, inserted, reordered, blocked, repeated, or abandoned steps
  + [semantic_surprise] records meaning, dependency, identity, or boundary discovered only through actual work
  + [routine_update_candidate] proposes a revised SOP routine, estimate, trigger, or review point
  + [training_example] may project reviewed intent, diff, disposition, and next-plan quality into a later corpus
  = must: require review before adopting a lesson as durable routine or model-training evidence
  - never: make hindsight appear to have been the original plan

& [CalendarRepositoryJoin] binds planned time to actual history
  + each scheduled task points to one TaskContract, plan revision, repository snapshot, and expected ChangeCapsule set
  + each wake event loads exact versions and first checks whether assumptions, authority, targets, and relevance remain current
  + each completed or missed block records actual work and reason without silently changing the scheduled record
  + rear reflection may produce duration, dependency, review, risk, and recurrence update candidates
  + Planner consumes admitted updates to revise future uncommitted schedule alternatives
  = must: preserve external calendar synchronization as a separately authorized effect

& [ExistingSupport] is broad but incomplete
  + [available] is typed temporal graph vocabulary, Planner temporal projections, semantic state and transitions, pertinent history, reentry, notifications, faculty cycles, task contracts, signed snapshots, trust, query, narrative, and Git-backed project evidence
  + [Walking_Attention_available] is explicit forward frame, rear diff review, tandem exchange, reflection packets, checker gates, and no-hidden-attention boundary
  + [missing] is general CalendarItem, recurrence, availability, schedule solver, temporal authority adapter, repository event schema, ChangeCapsule, bidirectional scheduler, compiler semantic-diff engine, retention and privacy implementation, and calendar provider integration
  = conclusion: form data and protocol authority before selecting storage, solver, calendar provider, or concurrent runtime

& [FirstProof] is a deterministic calendar-repository walk
  + [clock] is one logical-time fixture with explicit civil-time examples but no live clock dependency
  + [calendar] contains availability, one deadline, one review checkpoint, and one recurring candidate routine
  + [objective] decomposes into three dependent task steps with estimates and one reversible simulated effect
  + [forward] Planner schedules a candidate path and Worker produces one deliberate deviation
  + [journal] records every material task, tool, effect, review, and calendar transition
  + [rear] compares declared intent to actual diff, identifies the deviation and one newly exposed requirement, and refuses premature completion
  + [join] invalidates one prepared dependent step, revises the remaining plan, and releases the corrected next step
  + [compiler] performs textual, semantic, impact, target-correspondence, and proof diffs over one bounded SOP change
  + [replay] reproduces normalized schedule, ChangeCapsules, review decisions, and final admitted state
  + [negative] rejects stale version, unsourced time, mixed unrelated diff, missing reflection, fabricated atomic snapshot, and history rewrite

& [EvaluationSet] tests thoughtfulness rather than archive volume
  + [plan_quality] is feasibility, dependency satisfaction, deadline fit, slack, uncertainty, and user correction rate
  + [reflection_quality] is detected overreach, underreach, missing proof, requirement discovery, and false-positive rate
  + [semantic_diff_quality] is identity, relation, contract, authority, effect, and target impact precision and recall
  + [join_correctness] is stale-candidate rejection, invalidation, release, deadlock absence, and deterministic replay
  + [calendar_correctness] is timezone, recurrence, commitment state, trigger, miss, cancellation, and reschedule handling
  + [history_quality] is completeness, attribution, unrelated-state separation, compaction fidelity, and inspectability
  + [work] is journal volume, snapshot amplification, review latency, blocked forward time, compiler work, storage, and user attention

& [FaultSet] is mandatory
  + [calendar_as_plan] treats a candidate schedule as a user or external commitment
  + [false_urgency] converts estimate or proximity into authority or priority
  + [time_domain_collapse] confuses civil, UTC, monotonic, logical, valid, and transaction time
  + [moment_flood] preserves every insignificant event and obscures material change
  + [snapshot_overclaim] calls sequential observations one atomic world state
  + [history_rewrite] edits prior intent, plan, diff, or review to match later knowledge
  + [rear_rationalization] invents justification after the fact rather than identifying overreach
  + [forward_runaway] commits dependent work while applicable reflection is pending
  + [reflection_deadlock] prevents progress indefinitely without timeout, residual, or disposition
  + [shared_mutation_race] forward and rear lanes modify one state without version gates
  + [diff_surface_collapse] treats textual, semantic, behavioral, effect, and proof changes as equivalent
  + [unrelated_diff_mix] attributes another user, agent, process, or task change to the current work
  + [compiler_self_certification] lets generated artifacts prove their own correspondence
  + [calendar_privacy_leak] exposes participants, titles, locations, or routines beyond task purpose

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is CTPR-001 through CTPR-038
  + [CTPR-001] make Planner the central candidate-path and temporal coordination faculty
  + [CTPR-002] define Calendar as a versioned temporal commitment and wake-condition projection
  + [CTPR-003] distinguish objectives, dependencies, temporal constraints, effects, reviews, schedules, and commitments
  + [CTPR-004] define event, task, block, appointment, deadline, reminder, wake, recurrence, and review identities
  + [CTPR-005] distinguish civil, instant, monotonic, logical, valid, transaction, and uncertain time
  + [CTPR-006] preserve time source, zone, precision, interpretation, and uncertainty
  + [CTPR-007] integrate Planner, Weaver, all review faculties, Calendar, Worker, and rear reflection
  + [CTPR-008] preserve forecast, commitment, execution, miss, cancellation, and supersession separately
  + [CTPR-009] build an append-only event journal and content-addressed snapshot graph
  + [CTPR-010] preserve Git as a projection rather than the only runtime repository
  + [CTPR-011] record every materially observable transition under an explicit cadence policy
  + [CTPR-012] aggregate or expire non-material micro-events under inspectable retention
  + [CTPR-013] define ChangeCapsule as intent, actual, semantic, justification, support, requirement, calendar, compiler, review, and state delta
  + [CTPR-014] separate unrelated dirty or external state from attributed work
  + [CTPR-015] map Walking Attention forward, rear, tandem, diff, and reentry forms with fidelity records
  + [CTPR-016] preserve Walking Attention source authority and non-imported hidden-state claims
  + [CTPR-017] run prospective, execution, and retrospective lanes against exact immutable versions
  + [CTPR-018] allow prepared-ahead candidate work without allowing dependent effect commitment before review
  + [CTPR-019] invalidate or remask prepared work when rear review changes its premises
  + [CTPR-020] define bounded reflection lag, timeout, residual, and no-deadlock behavior
  + [CTPR-021] use compare-and-append versioning at every forward-rear join
  + [CTPR-022] give the compiler distinct forward parse, resolve, lower, and project stages
  + [CTPR-023] give the compiler distinct rear source, semantic, impact, correspondence, and proof reviews
  + [CTPR-024] keep textual, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, and proof diffs distinct
  + [CTPR-025] compute invalidation across IR, indexes, packages, schedules, workflows, models, tools, and hardware targets
  + [CTPR-026] require Observer reconciliation before admitting a compiled package family
  + [CTPR-027] use reviewed forecast error, plan deviation, and semantic surprise as candidate future lessons
  + [CTPR-028] forbid hindsight from rewriting declared intent or prior plans
  + [CTPR-029] bind scheduled work to TaskContract, plan revision, repository state, and expected review
  + [CTPR-030] revalidate assumptions, authority, targets, and relevance at calendar wake
  + [CTPR-031] treat external calendar synchronization as a separately authorized effect
  + [CTPR-032] define privacy and retention for calendar, journal, snapshots, diffs, and learned examples
  + [CTPR-033] prove one deterministic calendar-repository forward-rear walk before live scheduling
  + [CTPR-034] prove one bounded dual-pass SOP compiler diff in the same fixture
  + [CTPR-035] reject stale versions, unsourced time, mixed diffs, missing reflection, false snapshots, and history rewrite
  + [CTPR-036] measure planning, reflection, semantic diff, join, calendar, history, work, and user-attention quality
  + [CTPR-037] preserve exact deterministic fallback when the Planner model, calendar provider, or rear model is absent
  + [CTPR-038] preserve current language, tool, service, workspace, calendar, and effect authority until separate activation

& [Decision] is preserve the central temporal and reflective runtime candidate
  + [architecture_fit] is high because Calendar, Planner, repository history, Walking Attention, Operator Shell, and incremental compiler all meet at TaskContract and ChangeCapsule
  + [canonical_authority] current SOP, faculty, history, reentry, notification, trust, compiler, Operator Shell, and Walking Attention authorities remain separate within their signed scopes
  + [new_canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [calendar_provider_authority] is absent
  + [Walking_Attention_import_authority] is absent
  + [schedule_effect] add CTPR-SJS-01 after SMTC language-purpose reconciliation and make it a prerequisite to COS Operator Shell implementation
  + [first_candidate_after_authority] is one deterministic logical-calendar, event-repository, forward-rear, and dual-pass compiler fixture
  + [reasoning_depth] cross-project semantic import, temporal data, concurrency, compiler correspondence, retention, and effect boundaries require deeper architecture reasoning; a closed logical-time fixture becomes Spark-suitable after signed activation authority
